ore_margin_vs_hist":0.0,"_gate_piotroski":1,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":11.1,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.16653187624687438,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":100.0,"_gate_rev_durability":-0.007618638652195253,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":21.2,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.04122939691433001,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":56.9,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.011670753768599607,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":64.6,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.008151296458680355,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":86.4,"_gate_insider_own":0.27032,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Jefferies Financial Group Inc. operates as an investment banking and capital markets firm in the Americas, Europe, the Middle East, and the Asia-Pacific. It operates in two segments, Investment Banking and Capital Markets, and Asset Management. The company provides investment banking and advisory services for mergers or acquisitions, debt financing, restructurings, and private capital advisory transactions; underwriting and placement services related to corporate debt, municipal debt, mortgage-backed and asset-backed securities, equity and equity-linked securities, and loan syndication services; and corporate lending services. It also offers financing, securities lending, and other prime brokerage services; equities research, sales, and trading services; wealth management services; and online foreign exchange trading services. In addition, the company provides investment-grade distressed debt securities, U.S. and European government and agency securities, municipal bonds, leveraged loans, emerging markets debt, interest rates, and credit index derivative products; and manages and offers services to a diverse group of alternative asset management platforms across a spectrum of investment strategies and asset classes. It serves public companies, private companies, sponsors and owners, institutional investors, and government entities. The company was formerly known as Leucadia National Corporation and changed its name to Jefferies Financial Group Inc. in May 2018. Jefferies Financial Group Inc. was founded in 1962 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Richard Brian Handler | CEO & Director | Age 64 | Compensation: $11.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 7K people. Revenue per employee of $1.5M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 15%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $12K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Jefferies Financial Group Inc. is a large-cap financial services business with a $10.5B market cap on $10.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +15% over the past three years and -1% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 21% against a 11% cost of capital \u2014 a 10-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The company is burning through $1.7B of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 1.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 27% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 1.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 59% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.5924068997437453},{"text":"Piotroski score 1/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 11% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Large open-market insider purchases (net $318.7M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","16 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Investment Analysts\u2019 Weekly Ratings Changes for Zimmer Biomet (ZBH)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/investment-analysts-weekly-ratings-changes-for-zimmer-biomet-zbh.html","date":"2026-11-14","timestamp":1794617813.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.077,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Analysts\u2019 Weekly Ratings Updates for Generac (GNRC)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/analysts-weekly-ratings-updates-for-generac-gnrc.html","date":"2026-11-14","timestamp":1794616008.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.178,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"GlobalFoundries (NASDAQ:GFS) Stock: Insider Samak Azar Sells 335 Shares","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/globalfoundries-nasdaqgfs-stock-insider-samak-azar-sells-335-shares-3.html","date":"2026-11-14","timestamp":1794615774.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.896,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"LivaNova (NASDAQ:LIVN) CFO Alex Shvartsburg Sells 2,500 Shares of Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/livanova-nasdaqlivn-cfo-alex-shvartsburg-sells-2500-shares-of-stock.html","date":"2026-11-14","timestamp":1794614973.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.91,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["leadership"]},{"title":"Molina Healthcare (NYSE:MOH) Director Sells 1,600 Shares of Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","